  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>95649480e2feab4860af7b67e8696920</srcmd5>
    <version>0.18.0</version>
    <time>1786543946</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.18.0

Upstream minor release. The API surface is purely additive: an AST diff over
the whole module tree shows no public symbols removed and 18 added. One new
runtime dependency, psutil, is added to Requires; no existing floor moved.

Please take this together with python-vllm 0.27.1, submitted alongside it.
python-vllm previously carried an exact &quot;= 0.17.1&quot; requirement on this
package, which would have made it uninstallable the moment 0.18.0 landed;
that companion submission replaces the exact pin with a floor, so the two are
compatible in either order once both are in.

For the record on that pairing: vLLM upstream still pins compressed-tensors
== 0.17.0 on both v0.27.1 and main, so upstream has not itself adopted
0.18.0. All 15 symbols vllm imports from compressed_tensors were checked and
are present in both 0.17.1 and 0.18.0, with no removals, so the mismatch is a
version string rather than an API break.

There is still no %check. The previous comment justified that by saying
transformers was absent from Factory, which is no longer true; the real
reason is that python-torch is disabled on aarch64, so an import smoke test
would turn this noarch package into a build failure on every other
architecture. The comment now says so.

Verified on aarch64: build green, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1370784</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>54686c471ff078769d0212ceb3f65131</srcmd5>
    <version>0.19.0</version>
    <time>1790585214</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-compressed-tensors to 0.19.0.

One user-visible breaking change: GPTQ group/dynamic activation ordering
has been removed. actorder=&quot;group&quot;/&quot;dynamic&quot; and actorder=True now raise
a ValueError instead of warning; actorder=&quot;weight&quot; is the replacement.
Observer resolution and the automatic qstrategy inference have moved to
llm-compressor, so qargs must be passed explicitly.

Note on the release notes: they list &quot;transformers&gt;=5.16 is now required&quot;
under Breaking Changes, but that is a @requires_version test-skip decorator
(PR 848 modifies only tests/). The shipped src/ has no version gate and
PKG-INFO still declares transformers&gt;=4.45.0, so the spec floor is
unchanged.

Runtime dependencies are unchanged: setup.py declares the same five
(torch&gt;=2.10.0, transformers&gt;=4.45.0, pydantic&gt;=2.0, loguru, psutil) as
0.18.0. accelerate remains an extra and the new dev/docs extras are not
packaged. No subpackage change - python313/python314-compressed-tensors as
before.

Built natively on aarch64 against openSUSE:Factory:ARM. The
openSUSE:Tumbleweed project is a kernel/qemu project with no python-torch
or python-transformers, so it cannot resolve this package's build
requires. rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness, identical to the 0.18.0 baseline.
%check remains disabled, pre-existing and GPU-dependent.

Caveat for the reviewer: openSUSE:Factory currently has a
python-huggingface-hub 2.0.0 / python-transformers collision that makes
&quot;import transformers&quot; fail at runtime. compressed-tensors does not import
transformers at build time, so this build is unaffected, but the resulting
RPM is inert at runtime until python-transformers is fixed.

No open bugs and no VUL- bugs against this package; no HF CVE in the
crossed range reaches compressed-tensors' shipped code.
</comment>
    <requestid>1380864</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
